From 8ffa49d0c6efe4d8f826129dcd3f2d0092350638 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patch-author <a@a.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 07:20:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Patch 0377: fix DLC pet display -- Ruby Dragonling would've
 shown blank

- New DlcManager.petDef(id), same fallback shape as heroClassDef: base
  PET_BY_ID first, then any installed pack's own pets.
- Fixed 4 real UI call sites that were still reading base-only
  PET_BY_ID directly for an already-owned pet's display data:
  HatchRevealModal (the actual hatch-reveal screen), HatcheryPanel
  (Nests tab card), PetEnlargedModal, IdleView (equipped companion).
  A hatched Ruby Dragonling would have shown as blank/'Unnamed' in all
  four before this patch.
- TestingPanel.tsx now lists DlcManager.allPets() so DLC pets can be
  test-spawned directly.
- StatsPanel.tsx's 'Pet breeds collected' deliberately left reading the
  base PETS array -- same reasoning ALL_PETS_COLLECTED's own achievement
  check already applies (a base-game completionist stat shouldn't
  require owning DLC to complete).
- Verified: tsc --noEmit, vite build, electron-builder --linux dir
  package build, a direct runtime test confirming petDef() resolves a
  DLC pet/base pet/unknown id correctly, and a full-tree grep confirming
  no other PET_BY_ID[...] lookup remains outside the two intentional
  ones.
